infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Type hints: TypeScript enforces, Python only describes
  desc Both erase types at runtime — but a TS type error blocks the build, while a Python program runs regardless
  compares
    - label TypeScript types
      children
        - label Erased at runtime
          desc Types vanish once compiled to JS, no runtime check
        - label tsc fails the build
          desc A type error normally blocks compilation
        - label Bad code does not ship
          desc The build gate is the enforcement
        - label Checked at compile time
          desc Part of the standard build step
    - label Python hints (PEP 484)
      children
        - label Ignored at runtime
          desc The interpreter never validates them
        - label Program runs anyway
          desc Wrong types run until a value breaks
        - label Stored in __annotations__
          desc Advisory metadata, not a guard
        - label Checked only by mypy / pyright
          desc A separate tool you must run in CI
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
